```java
public class Account {
    // STATIC binding: private (not inherited → compile-time only)
    private void audit() { System.out.println("Account audit"); }

    // STATIC binding: static (class-level → no vtable)
    public static String getPolicy() { return "Standard Policy"; }

    // STATIC binding: final (sealed → no override)
    public final String getAccountId() { return "ACC-BASE"; }

    // DYNAMIC binding: instance method (can be overridden → vtable dispatch)
    public String getDescription() { return "Generic Account"; }

    // STATIC binding: overloaded methods (compiler picks by arg types)
    public void deposit(BigDecimal amount) { }              // overload 1
    public void deposit(BigDecimal amount, String note) { } // overload 2

    public void callAudit() { audit(); }  // audit() is private → static binding
}

public class SavingsAccount extends Account {
    // OVERRIDES: dynamic binding at runtime
    @Override public String getDescription() { return "Savings Account"; }

    // HIDES: static binding at compile-time (NOT override!)
    public static String getPolicy() { return "Savings Policy"; }
}
```

Which binding for each method type:

```java
Account ref = new SavingsAccount();

// ═══ DYNAMIC BINDING (runtime — actual type = SavingsAccount) ═══
ref.getDescription();
// Compiler: Account.getDescription() exists? YES → valid.
// Runtime: JVM checks actual type → SavingsAccount → vtable → SavingsAccount.getDescription()
// Result: "Savings Account" ← Child's version! Dynamic dispatch.

// ═══ STATIC BINDING (compile-time — reference type = Account) ═══

// private method:
ref.callAudit();
// callAudit() calls audit() → private → static binding → Account.audit()
// Private methods are NOT in vtable — no dynamic dispatch possible.

// static method:
ref.getPolicy();
// Compiler: ref is Account → Account.getPolicy() → "Standard Policy"
// Static methods resolved at compile-time by reference type. No vtable.

// final method:
ref.getAccountId();
// Compiler: final → cannot be overridden → binds directly to Account.getAccountId()
// JVM can inline final methods for performance.

// overloaded method:
ref.deposit(amount);           // compiler picks overload 1 (BigDecimal)
ref.deposit(amount, "Salary"); // compiler picks overload 2 (BigDecimal, String)
// Overload resolution happens at COMPILE TIME based on argument types.
```

HOW the vtable works internally:

```java
// JVM creates a vtable (virtual method table) for each class at class loading time.
// The vtable maps method signatures to actual method implementations.

// Account vtable:
// getDescription() → Account.getDescription
// deposit(BigDecimal) → Account.deposit

// SavingsAccount vtable:
// getDescription() → SavingsAccount.getDescription  ← OVERRIDDEN!
// deposit(BigDecimal) → Account.deposit              ← inherited (same)

// When: Account ref = new SavingsAccount()
// ref.getDescription() → JVM looks at ref's actual object → SavingsAccount
// → checks SavingsAccount's vtable → getDescription() → SavingsAccount.getDescription()
// This is "virtual method invocation" or "dynamic dispatch."

// private/static/final methods are NOT in the vtable:
// → resolved at compile time → no vtable lookup → faster!
// That's why JVM can optimize final methods (inlining).
```

